WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.780
Speaker 1: Let's start today with Vladimir
Putin and Russia.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.000
We know that Russian casualties are mounting.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
We know that Russia is being drastically affected
by sanctions, even if they are undertaking

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.609
a public relations campaign to try to make
the case that they're fine and everything's

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:20.689
fine.

00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:29.650
And the latest in this seemingly interminable
fiasco is Putin and Russia claiming that the

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:36.430
United States is actually behind an alleged
Ukrainian drone attack, which I guess damaged

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:44.050
a flagpole and did nothing else, whereas intelligence
analysts are saying it is far more likely

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:49.660
that this is a Russian false flag than it
is something with American involvement, particularly

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.340
because it failed so badly.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.250
If indeed the goal was to hurt somebody.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:00.039
And it's just blatantly pathetic in terms
of the video that has been released.

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:01.570
So let's go through this in pieces.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.500
NBC News Report.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.900
Russia claims the U.S. is behind the alleged
Ukrainian drone attack on the Kremlin.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:15.409
Both Kiev and Washington strongly denied involvement
in what Moscow said without citing evidence

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:20.690
was an attempt to assassinate President Vladimir
Putin.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:24.900
Russia claimed Thursday the U.S. was behind
the alleged drone attack on the Kremlin and

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.820
said it was a Ukrainian attempt to kill Putin.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.640
This accusation was made without citing any
evidence.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.270
A less than 24 hours after Moscow said that
it foiled an overnight drone strike on a building

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.600
that is the heart of the country's government
and Putin's residence.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.219
Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov, quite a note
of disinformation claimed Thursday that Washington

00:01:46.219 --> 00:01:49.330
masterminded and masterminded the incident.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:54.250
The U.S. swiftly rejected the accusation,
saying it had nothing to do with it, as did

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.250
Ukraine.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:01.780
Now there is another very interesting piece,
a CNBC slash NBC report.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.850
Analysts say Russia, quote, likely staged
Kremlin drone attack it blamed on Ukraine

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.259
and the west.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.980
Speculation is mounting that Russia staged
the drone attack on the kremlin that it blamed

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.010
on Ukraine, with political analysts saying
there are a number of reasons why the alleged

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.290
strike, which Russia called a planned terrorist
attack, just doesn't add up.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:24.680
Russia accused Ukraine of attempting to attack
the Kremlin, saying the government in Kiev

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.930
tried to strike at the heart of Russia's government.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:32.360
Russian President Putin wasn't injured in
what it characterized as an assassination

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.360
attempt.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.160
In fact, Putin had not been in the Kremlin
at the time of the alleged incident, but provided

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.120
no evidence Ukraine carried it out.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.640
Ukraine denied involvement.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.930
Russia has often been accused of plotting
false flag attacks that it can blame on Ukraine

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:51.420
and use to justify or escalate its own military
aggression against the country as the war

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.560
drags on into its 15 month.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.280
So what do we actually know?

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:02.160
I mean, we know that there was something on
video that looks like a drone.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.430
It appears as though it hit a flagpole.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:12.459
Moscow claims it was Ukraine trying to kill
Putin, masterminded by the United States.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:14.670
There's no evidence of that.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.879
Ukraine denies it.

00:03:15.879 --> 00:03:17.780
The U.S. denies it.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.360
Analysts say it was likely staged.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.690
Now, let's believe it for a second.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:27.540
And what I mean by that is let's believe for
a second that this really was an attempt by

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.810
Ukraine masterminded by the United States
to kill Putin.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.129
Couple of different things.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:40.239
One, we have to believe that an attack masterminded
by the United States and carried out by Ukraine

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:41.640
hit a flagpole.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.830
Okay.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:47.470
Not the most predictable outcome that we would
imagine.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:55.220
And or secondly, we have to believe that Russia
is admitting that their air defense system

00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:01.659
is so poor that enemy drones now just fly
over the Capitol and hit a flagpole at the

00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:02.659
Kremlin.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:06.840
Both of these scenarios certainly taken together.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.110
Aren't super easy to believe.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:14.870
And what we do know is that there's a very
long history with Vladimir Putin of false

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:21.009
flag type events of this kind used to justify
whatever.

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:26.410
And you can go all the way back to Putin's
ascension to power with examples of that,

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.950
probably a topic for another day.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:34.449
What we know is that Russia continues to have
huge losses.

00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:39.889
Russia believed this would be super easy when
it started last year, 15 months ago.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:47.040
And it's probably not easy to keep the Russian
public patriotic and happy as family members

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.670
and friends and loved ones, etc., are being
killed as a result of what was supposed to

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.650
be a very easy takeover of Ukraine.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:05:02.860
So from a PR perspective, it would be extraordinarily
useful to be able to credibly claim that the

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.479
Ukraine with a masterminded by the United
States, Ukraine carried out such an attack

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:08.830
or attempted attack.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.789
And the key line in all of this is that Russia
says it will respond.

00:05:12.789 --> 00:05:13.900
What is a response mean?

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.020
What will that response look like?

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:20.289
Well, we don't know yet, but that often is
the name of the game.

00:05:20.289 --> 00:05:27.940
Create a pretext, a surface, a pretext to
then justify further escalations and maybe

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:33.270
have a PR impact to get more people on the
side of this completely harebrained incursion

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.180
by Putin and Ukraine.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:40.789
When you ask me how will it end, I still have
absolutely no idea, but it's looking like

00:05:40.789 --> 00:07:03.849
it's going to be relatively ugly.

